WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:54.393
[Music]

00:00:56.260 --> 00:01:02.126
[Narrator:] On a modest farm, far out from town, Lucy X had been living with her aunt for two years.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:07.200
Two years of refusing to believe that she was sick with tuberculosis.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:11.200
She was constantly tired and couldn't seem to get rid of a cough.

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:14.833
Still, she had forced herself to stay up to keep working on the farm.

00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:20.333
But one day the pump handle was too heavy, and the water bucket an unbearable load.

00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:22.253
That terrible cough again.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:28.360
[Music]

00:01:28.366 --> 00:01:29.886
The taste of blood.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.460
[Music]

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:36.580
Aunt Martha was frightened.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:43.480
She should have taken Lucy to a doctor long ago, but Lucy was so terribly afraid of doctors.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:53.600
Aunt Martha called the family doctor immediately and arranged to send her to his office for a complete checkup.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:02:05.033
After the doctor had finished a complete physical examination and learned the case history, he sent Lucy home telling her not to worry.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:06.999
But the doctor was worried.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.666
That was advanced tuberculosis.

00:02:09.666 --> 00:02:15.706
Immediate sanatorium treatment was her only chance, and he knew the family could not afford such expense.

00:02:17.266 --> 00:02:20.832
Then he thought of the Tuberculosis Association.

00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:26.966
The field worker in the Tuberculosis Association was glad to help in obtaining hospitalization for Lucy.

00:02:26.966 --> 00:02:35.446
On the doctor's suggestion, she prepared at once to call on the family and to attempt to arrange with the authorities for Lucy's care.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.940
Cooperation with physicians and public authorities  in meeting the difficult problems of patients

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:49.220
is part of the responsibility of Tuberculosis Associations.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:52.646
The public expects it, rightfully.

00:02:52.866 --> 00:03:00.566
Each year millions of people buy Tuberculosis Christmas seals to help protect their homes from this deadly contagion.

00:03:00.566 --> 00:03:05.899
Tuberculosis Associations accept this money and spend it on their scientific [?].

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:10.733
It is a plus symbolized by the double-barred cross.

00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:15.799
The field worker told Aunt Martha that tax-supported institutions now care for persons

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:19.900
who have tuberculosis in order to keep the disease from spreading.

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:25.200
Hospitalization of one tuberculosis patient may prevent many new cases.

00:03:32.033 --> 00:03:36.033
She told Lucy of sanatoriums where complete bed rest was possible,

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:41.966
of wonderful equipment which had been perfected to help persons who were fighting tuberculosis.

00:03:41.966 --> 00:03:45.566
All of these were available for Lucy.

00:03:45.566 --> 00:03:48.466
Lucy wanted to be left with her Aunt Martha.

00:03:48.466 --> 00:03:53.432
She offered to stay in bed, do anything the doctor advised, if she could stay at home.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:56.299
The field worker explained that this was not enough.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:01.700
The specialized work of the tuberculosis sanatorium cannot be done in a home.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:14.160
Finally, Lucy consented to go, but it was the decision of a sick person too weak to resist longer,

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:18.260
not the cooperation of one who has hope.

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:30.360
[Music]

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:36.300
It was late that night when the field worker's car turned into the sanatorium drive.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:42.600
She'd called in advance and had arranged with the night supervisor to have a room ready for the patient.

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:46.000
The sanatorium staff feel deep sympathy for the emergency cases,

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:54.280
the people who have waited too long, for the staff well knows how deadly delays can be.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:05:03.120
[Music]

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:09.680
[Music changes to a jauntier rhythm]

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:14.960
While Lucy was still sleeping, the floor nurse was preparing to care for her.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:22.733
Working directly over the sick person, the nurse might breathe the tuberculosis germs into her own lungs.

00:05:22.733 --> 00:05:32.699
For that reason, she wears a mask over her nose and mouth, and the sterile gown over her uniform.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:35.400
The nurse knew that her first task that morning

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:40.440
was to make Lucy feel that the sanatorium staff were her friends, and wanted to help her.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:43.140
That was of primary importance.

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:56.000
She must also teach her to hold a tissue over her mouth to keep her from spreading the germs.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:06:01.133
Years before, Lucy had been in a sanatorium where her mother was a patient.

00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:05.799
Her examination had shown that she had tuberculosis in an early form.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:08.900
The disease cannot be inherited.

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:14.033
Lucy had probably taken it from her own mother in the daily contact of the household.

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:17.666
Her mother died before Lucy could be placed in a sanatorium.

00:06:17.666 --> 00:06:22.066
After that, terror-stricken, Lucy refused to go.

00:06:22.066 --> 00:06:25.566
To her, sanatoriums meant death.

00:06:25.566 --> 00:06:27.932
She had then fled to her aunt's farm.

00:06:27.933 --> 00:06:33.973
She thought fresh air would cure tuberculosis, but it had not cured.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:38.200
Rest is the key element in the cure for tuberculosis.

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:45.433
Rest, highly specialized rest, such as can be supplied only in a proper hospital.

00:06:45.433 --> 00:06:48.299
But Lucy had no faith in the sanatorium.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.566
Her mother had died in one.

00:06:50.566 --> 00:06:55.632
She didn't realize that the mother was already fatally sick with tuberculosis when she went there.

00:06:55.633 --> 00:06:58.833
That it was too late then.

00:06:58.833 --> 00:07:02.993
Hot with fever and indifferent, she submitted to the examination.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:08.660
For a diagnosis of her case, the doctor needed to know not only the damage done to her lungs,

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.880
but also her complete physical condition.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:16.973
Whether the sanatorium could cure Lucy now was a question they could not yet answer.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:24.100
Their first job was to show her that the sanatorium is a place of great hope.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:30.760
The doctor asked the nurse to encourage Lucy to eat a good breakfast, and then to prepare her for a chest x-ray.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:54.480
[Music]

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:58.833
In a sanatorium, food is of the utmost importance.

00:07:58.833 --> 00:08:02.233
It is scientifically selected and prepared.

00:08:02.233 --> 00:08:06.799
Patients in various stages of recovery need different foods.

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:10.380
The dietician who plans the meals takes this into consideration.

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:16.660
Fresh fruits and vegetables, milk and eggs, all of these are body builders.

00:08:16.666 --> 00:08:24.732
And with tuberculosis, the problem is just that: to heal those portions of the body destroyed by disease.

00:08:24.733 --> 00:08:28.653
This is one part of the specialized work which the sanatorium offers.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:42.260
[Music]

00:08:42.266 --> 00:08:45.766
Another phase is done by technicians in the laboratories,

00:08:45.766 --> 00:08:50.606
whose studies help the doctors in determining the exact conditions of their patients.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.680
And then came the x-rays.

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:57.333
X-ray is like a flash of lightning that momentarily lights up the lungs

00:08:57.333 --> 00:09:02.113
so that a shadow picture can be made of the lung tissue itself.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:28.740
[Music]

00:09:28.940 --> 00:09:36.400
An expert x-ray technician makes the picture and only a specialist can rightly interpret it.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:41.700
A doctor who know how to read such a picture can tell much about the progress of the disease

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:45.720
and can decide from that what kind of treatment to undertake.

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:56.600
The medical staff studied the x-ray film, comparing it with one sent from the other sanatorium

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.440
that had been taken at time her mother was there.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:04.160
The first one showed early minimal disease had just started.

00:10:04.166 --> 00:10:10.099
Now there was a hole in her lung where the disease had eaten away part of the lung tissue.

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:13.566
This was advanced pulmonary tuberculosis.

00:10:13.566 --> 00:10:16.632
Those months on the farm had taken a toll.

00:10:16.633 --> 00:10:22.266
The doctors decided that surgery might save the lung, but Lucy was too weak now for an operation.

00:10:22.266 --> 00:10:26.486
To build up her strength, complete bed rest was prescribed.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:34.533
[Music]

00:10:34.533 --> 00:10:39.833
Day after day, Lucy grew steadily weaker because she had no will to live.

00:10:39.833 --> 00:10:45.713
During her regular rounds one night, her nurse stopped in Lucy's room,

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:01.380
and then came directly to the doctor's office.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:04.980
"Lucy seems worse," the nurse reported.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:14.733
Every physician knows that the mental state of a patient can adversely influence the physical.

00:11:14.733 --> 00:11:21.013
To deal with such a problem is not simple, and to succeed requires more than a knowledge of medicine.

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:31.840
Lucy must want to get well and believe that she could get well.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:43.860
Outside of the nurses' station, Lucy's nurse waited anxiously.

00:11:43.866 --> 00:11:48.946
All the sanatorium staff are deeply concerned if a patient loses the will to fight.

00:11:55.540 --> 00:12:02.433
The doctor tried to tell Lucy that she must look beyond the few years here at the sanatorium to the life that awaited her.

00:12:02.433 --> 00:12:06.333
A normal life that any young girl should enjoy.

00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:10.433
There should be work, play, romance.

00:12:13.360 --> 00:12:20.760
Beyond these [?] months waited all the years that could be shaped into useful living.

00:12:20.766 --> 00:12:30.966
[Music]

00:12:33.460 --> 00:12:36.800
As the night wore on, he struck the right chord.

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:40.100
The listless mask broke; Lucy looked up and smiled.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:42.000
"Yes," she whispered.

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.966
She would try to get well.

00:12:43.966 --> 00:12:46.566
She believed she could get well.

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:01.960
Lucy cooperated and steadily improved.

00:13:01.966 --> 00:13:08.266
She became strong enough so that some surgery to close the lung cavity could be applied.

00:13:08.266 --> 00:13:10.832
Pneumothorax treatments were begun.

00:13:10.833 --> 00:13:17.933
A pneumo, as they call it, temporarily collapses the lung so that it can rest and heal itself.

00:13:17.933 --> 00:13:25.133
To collapse the lung in this way, air is injected through a needle into the chest, but outside of the lung sac.

00:13:25.133 --> 00:13:31.999
This gradually forces the lung up into smaller space so that it will have a chance to heal.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:39.200
The other lung does the necessary work of breathing for the body, while the collapsed lung lies still.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:41.900
A broken leg could not be healed with constant exercise.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:47.580
Neither can an ulcer and a lung be healed while the lung continues in full motion of breathing.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:55.933
At first these pneumos are given every day, later every two weeks.

00:13:55.933 --> 00:13:58.499
The procedure is done under a local anesthetic.

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.033
There is no pain.

00:14:00.033 --> 00:14:03.433
It requires but a few minutes of time.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:08.540
[Music]

00:14:10.140 --> 00:14:16.860
For pneumothorax treatment, a fluoroscope is used to study the lung's condition.

00:14:16.866 --> 00:14:19.766
The degree of collapse can be observed by the doctors.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:24.620
After some months, Lucy's sputum carried no more tuberculosis germs.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:31.500
Then she was moved to a two-bedroom with Ann, a girl who was at the same stage of treatment.

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:37.000
Lucy's body must remain at complete rest for months to come, but not her mind.

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:47.520
The sanatorium's Educational Director now joined 
the medical staff in working for Lucy's recovery.

00:14:49.966 --> 00:14:55.246
[Music]

00:14:55.480 --> 00:15:04.040
In sanatorium, patients are permitted to complete formal schooling interrupted by their isolation in the hospital.

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:23.473
[Music]

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:27.000
It isn't enough to find the patient a book.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:30.500
That book should help him towards some definite 
goal.

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:34.733
For Lucy, that goal is fashion designing.

00:15:34.733 --> 00:15:44.933
[Music]

00:15:45.300 --> 00:15:50.600
In the meantime, Lucy was eagerly completing one high school subject after another.

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:57.260
[Music]

00:15:57.266 --> 00:16:01.099
Being allowed up for meals was the next big step for Lucy.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:05.266
Both she and Ann had been transferred to the up-patient wing of the sanatorium

00:16:05.266 --> 00:16:09.886
where they were allowed to go to the dining room for one meal a day.

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:17.960
Even in this stage of improvement, afternoon rest hours were important.

00:16:17.966 --> 00:16:24.299
The body needed rest to repair the lung tissue that tuberculosis had destroyed.

00:16:24.300 --> 00:16:31.440
So work towards high school diploma and fashion designing had to be done within strict limitations.

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:41.733
Although it would be months before she could leave the sanatorium,

00:16:41.733 --> 00:16:47.199
plans began for that day when she would reenter the world and look for a job.

00:16:47.200 --> 00:16:50.600
This is called rehabilitation.

00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:55.600
In some instances, rehabilitation means the teaching of a new trade.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:17:00.040
In Lucy's case, it meant finishing high school and choosing a vocation.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:06.060
[Music]

00:17:06.066 --> 00:17:11.799
When she had completed the last course necessary for high school graduation, they brought her a diploma.

00:17:11.800 --> 00:17:17.566
Diplomas are usually presented on platforms while a large audience of friends look on.

00:17:17.566 --> 00:17:22.432
Aunt Martha and her teacher were the only audience on Lucy's graduation day.

00:17:22.433 --> 00:17:24.833
But it was hard to tell who was the most pleased.

00:17:24.833 --> 00:17:28.093
That was a very special day.

00:17:28.200 --> 00:17:40.080
[Music]

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:47.360
But the real triumph came when Lucy was healed and ready to go back into the world.

00:17:47.366 --> 00:17:52.999
There was a time when sanatorium patients, after several idle years, were simply released.

00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:58.100
No guidance in finding jobs, few friends to help them make contact.,

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:04.800
Such persons often returned to the sanatorium within a few years, broken in body and spirit.

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:11.000
Because sanatoriums have learned from these tragedies,

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:14.900
they now begin planning for the patient from the first day of treatment.

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:20.460
In Lucy's case, the sanatorium staff had kept her in touch with the outside world.

00:18:20.466 --> 00:18:24.299
She wasn't being turned out of the sanatorium with no place to go.

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:28.500
She had a goal and practical training to reach it.

00:18:29.300 --> 00:19:21.600
[Music]

00:19:21.600 --> 00:19:28.833
The rehabilitation agent will continue to be her counselor.

00:19:28.833 --> 00:19:34.233
"Remember," the doctor cautioned her, "you must come in often for a checkup."

00:19:34.233 --> 00:19:42.753
Therein lay her assurance, that in leaving the sanatorium she was not losing its protecting strength.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:56.033
The sanatorium stands ever-vigilant, healer of the sick, guardian of the public health.

00:19:56.033 --> 00:20:04.993
With such a friend, Lucy in happy confidence went out to strive for success, to achieve the life of a normal, healthy girl.

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:09.820
[Music]

